            <ArticleTitle>Parallel angioplasty dilatation catheter and guide wire: a new technique for the dilatation of calcified coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>72-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) of heavily calcified rigid coronary arteries has decreased success and increased complication rates. Three cases are presented describing a new technique for the dilatation of severely calcified coronary arteries that were not dilatable by conventional angioplasty methods. This technique involves the use of a balloon dilatation catheter system parallel to a guide wire.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
